35 #uuid "6c838d5e-1457-5ed8-957b-544017d2ddfe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066202 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186487926 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066202 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066202 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066202 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186487926 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066202 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "72c56336-2a3e-5cd0-b70e-c6cad4b4b776" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068495 #edb/ref 1069 "e-14246" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068495 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the solution to the equation $6^x - 6^5= 0?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068495 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4912a540-482c-51be-bdc4-8fb128ddfb77" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068495 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we isolate the term with the variable exponent by adding $6^5$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{6}^{x}-{6}^{5} & =0 \\\\ {6}^{x}-{6}^{5}+{6}^{5} & =0+{6}^{5} \\\\ {6}^{x}-\\cancel{{6}^{5}}+\\cancel{{6}^{5}} & =0+{6}^{5} \\\\ {6}^{x} & ={6}^{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince both sides of the equation share the same base $(6),$ we can equate the exponents. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{6}^{x} & ={6}^{5} \\\\ x & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${\\color{blue}x} = {\\color{blue}5}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068496 #edb/ref 1069 "e-14248" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068496 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the solution to $3^x = \\dfrac{1}{9}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068496 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bc9650d4-c12f-5e7a-b0b2-aacca9a9d698" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068496 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we rewrite $9$ as $3^2$ and then proceed as before:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3}^{x} & =\\frac{1}{9} \\\\ {3}^{x} & =\\frac{1}{{3}^{2}} \\\\ {3}^{x} & ={3}^{-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince both sides of the equation share the same base $(3),$ we equate the exponents and get $x=-2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068497 #edb/ref 1069 "e-14252" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068497 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve the equation $2\\cdot 3^x=54.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068497 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9a971439-a68b-58e5-a8f3-51045b2a0bf0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068497 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we divide both sides of the equation by $2\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot {3}^{x} & =54 \\\\ \\frac{2\\cdot {3}^{x}}{2} & =\\frac{54}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{2}\\cdot {3}^{x}}{\\cancel{2}} & =27 \\\\ {3}^{x} & =27\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite $27$ as $3^3$ so that both sides have the same base:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3}^{x}={3}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the exponents, we get ${\\color{blue}x}={\\color{blue}3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068731 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048725 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068731 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049714 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068731 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069155 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068731 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069474 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068731 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186488215 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068731 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186488218 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068731 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186488241 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068731 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186488279 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068731 #edb/ref 1039 "Solving an Exponential Equation" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068731 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186068495 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068731 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "f1e0a7d0-f891-5f5f-8d8d-1ced62b2899e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068732 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048262 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068732 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050495 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068732 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069156 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068732 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069157 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068732 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069358 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068732 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186488260 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068732 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186488284 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068732 #edb/ref 1039 "Solving an Exponential Equation by Changing the Base" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068732 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186068496 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068732 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "7e0c15b8-dc6e-570d-9392-4c679395cc87" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068733 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048673 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068733 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069122 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068733 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069158 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068733 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069523 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068733 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186488240 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068733 #edb/ref 1039 "Rearranging and Solving an Exponential Equation" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068733 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186068497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068733 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "368d83db-e01e-543b-ba45-8fc9c63242e9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068938 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069625 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068938 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069626 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068938 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069627 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068938 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069628 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068938 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069629 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068938 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068938 #edb/ref 1045 "Solving Exponential Equations" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068938 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186069625 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068938 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050511 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068938 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068938 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "155e5337-d5e8-53d9-b3b1-ee0f86219c05" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069158 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186066202 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069158 #edb/ref 1069 "q-223185" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069158 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069158 #edb/ref 1071 "If $2\\cdot {6}^{k}=72,$ then $k=${{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069158 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "82072348-e506-5a54-8f29-a9a2b212c19f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069158 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we isolate the term with the variable exponent by dividing both sides by $2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot {6}^{k} & =72 \\\\ \\frac{2\\cdot {6}^{k}}{2} & =\\frac{72}{2} \\\\ {6}^{k} & =36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rewrite $36$ as ${6}^{2}$ to get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{6}^{k} & =36 \\\\ {6}^{k} & ={6}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since both sides of the equation share the same base $(6)$, we equate the exponents:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{6}^{k} & ={6}^{2} \\\\ k & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $k=2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069625 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069626 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069625 #edb/ref 1061 170031 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069625 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ddaa7aab-6a5c-5c05-989d-9d15267eceec" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069625 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186070028 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069626 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069627 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069626 #edb/ref 1061 170032 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069626 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d2856989-c0e4-57bc-927d-5351b29a50a4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069626 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068731 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069627 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069628 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069627 #edb/ref 1061 170035 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069627 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "792c4b4f-5718-5101-aad6-254e3d0f1a1c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069627 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186070029 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069628 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069629 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069628 #edb/ref 1061 170036 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069628 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6ed2b746-5c94-5683-9d52-e609dd44d3af" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069628 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068732 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069629 #edb/ref 1061 170040 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069629 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a3c641ad-5eab-5dde-a062-3feb7d161f4c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069629 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068733 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186070028 #edb/ref 1064 "What is the value of $x$ that satisfies the following equation?\n\n$$\n3^x = 3^4\n$$\n\nWe call this an **exponential equation** because the variable is contained within the exponent. \n\nNow, this equation is pretty easy to solve. Because the bases on both sides of the equation are the same (they are both equal to $3$), we can simply equate the powers.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3}^{x} & ={3}^{4} \\\\ x & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to this equation is $x=4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186070028 #edb/ref 1065 8837 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186070028 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "1fc010d0-e380-5035-bdb6-5d5d7cff060b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186070028 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186070029 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's take a look at the following equation: \n\n$$\n5^x = 25\n$$\n\nWe can't solve this equation straight off the bat because the two sides of the equation don't share a common base.\n\nHowever, notice that $25$ can be written as a power of $5\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n25=5^2\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite the equation as\n\n$$\n5^x = 5^2.\n$$\n\nSince both sides of the equation are now written as an exponential expression with a common base of $5,$ we can set the exponents equal to each other and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{5}^{x} & ={5}^{2} \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo check that the solution is correct, we plug $x=2$ into the or